    "blisters": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "stack",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Blisters",
        "heading": "What dry feet do and don’t prevent",
        "lede": "<p>Waterproof socks help with blisters. They don’t prevent them, and anyone telling you otherwise is selling you something.</p>",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wet skin blisters more easily",
            "body": "<p>Soft, wet skin gives up under friction much faster than dry skin. Keeping your feet dry removes one of the three things a blister needs, and that’s a genuine help.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Friction and fit still matter",
            "body": "<p>The other two are pressure and movement. A boot that rubs will still rub. A sock that’s too small will still bunch up. No waterproof layer changes either.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Grit is the one nobody mentions",
            "body": "<p>On wet ground, fine grit washes in over the top and sits under your foot. It’s abrasive against your skin and against the sock. Rinse both at the end of a wet day.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "fit": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "wash",
        "layout": "panel",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Fit",
        "heading": "Check the boot before you order",
        "lede": "<p>This is the question most sellers skip and where most returns come from. Waterproof socks are thicker than the sock you’re used to.</p>",
        "link_label": "The sizes in centimetres",
        "link_url": "/pages/size-guide",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "About the same as a mid-weight sock",
            "body": "<p>If your boots are already snug with a thick walking sock, they’ll be tight with these. If you wear a thin liner under a thick sock, these replace both.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Between two sizes, go up",
            "body": "<p>Going down grips your toes, which is uncomfortable over eight hours and hard on the waterproof layer. Foot length, not shoe size, sets the size.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Your laces will need adjusting",
            "body": "<p>A thicker sock changes where a boot loads over the instep. Give the laces one honest adjustment on the first walk rather than deciding the fit is wrong.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
